{"name": "Champion Additions Control", "mod_id": "tfm2_champion_exclude", "author": "tfm2mods", "version": "0.6.2", "description": "Choose which unreleased champions will never be added by in-game season patches. Everything else about patches (balance changes, other new champions) works as normal.\n\n* Options > Gameplay > Champion Additions > Configure opens a window listing every champion not yet released in your save (base game and modded).\n* Click a champion to exclude it (red border). Excluded champions are taken out of the pool patches draw new champions from, so they are never released.\n* Exclude all = no new champions are ever added. Clear all = vanilla.\n* Class filter and champion name search.\n* Champions that are already released are never touched.\n\nThe list is stored per save (inside the save file - save the game to keep it). A save with no setting behaves like vanilla. The starting champion pool of a new game is not changed.\n\nBuilt for game 0.7.4. The mod hooks the game's patch-day code, so it is rebuilt for each game update; on any other game version the game disables it. Code mod (native DLL, Windows only). The window is in Korean when the game is set to Korean and in English otherwise.", "last_updated": "2026-11-25", "dependencies": [{"mod_id": "base", "version": ">=0.7.4, <0.7.5"}]}